haskell-ci has no hook for adding a step, so this patch adds one, and
cabal.haskell-ci points at it so that regenerating the workflow keeps it.
Applied by haskell-ci via plain patch(1), which takes the target file from
its command line, so the file names below are only documentation.

The step reports Core sizes for the derived Generic instances on every
compiler in the matrix; it is a measurement, not a check, so it is only ever
read out of the log. It costs ~10s, as the package is built by then.
--- a/.github/workflows/haskell-ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/haskell-ci.yml
@@ -269,6 +269,9 @@
       - name: build
         run: |
           $CABAL v2-build $ARG_COMPILER $ARG_TESTS $ARG_BENCH all --write-ghc-environment-files=always
+      - name: core size
+        run: |
+          PATH="$(dirname "$HC"):$PATH" bash ${PKGDIR_generics_sop}/bench/core-size.sh
       - name: tests
         run: |
           $CABAL v2-test $ARG_COMPILER $ARG_TESTS $ARG_BENCH all --test-show-details=direct
